>> title: Beef Stew, Slow Cooker
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, dinner, one-pot, braise, potatoes, slow cooker, crock pot
>> counters: The Slow Cooker
>> dish: beef-stew
>> kit: Slow Cooker
>> aka: beef stew, slow cooker beef stew, crockpot beef stew, crock pot stew
>> pairs-with: dinner-rolls
>> servings: 6
>> time: 8 hr 45 min
>> slack: forgiving — the potatoes are soft by hour six and stay soft, which is the trade this version makes for a day away
>> washing-up: the slow cooker crock, the skillet, a bowl to toss the beef with the flour in
>> capacity: 3 — the skillet, brown
>> keeps: 3 days — the beef is fine and the potatoes, eight hours in already, are grainy by the next morning

Two and a half cups of stock where the oven takes five. Nothing evaporates under this lid.

>> step: toss in the flour
Toss @beef chuck{3%lb}(1.4 kg; cut in 2-in cubes), @all-purpose flour{1/4%cup}(30 g), @kosher salt{2%tsp}, @black pepper{1%tsp}.

>> step: brown 12 min in a skillet, in batches
Brown @&(~1)floured beef{} in @vegetable oil{2%Tbs} in a #skillet{} for ~brown{12%min}, in two batches with room around each cube.

>> step: soften, deglaze the skillet clean
Soften @yellow onions{2%large}(chopped), @garlic{4%cloves}(minced) in the same skillet with @&(~1)browned beef{}, then pour in @dry red wine{1/2%cup}(120 mL) and scrape the base clean.

>> step: stew on low, 8 hr — everything in at once
Slow cook @&(~1)pot{} with @beef stock{2 1/2%cup}(590 mL), @thyme{4%sprigs}, @carrots{4%large}(cut in 2-in lengths), @Yukon Gold potatoes{2%lb}(900 g; quartered, skin on) in a #slow cooker{} on low for ~slow cook{8%hr}, lid on.

>> step: reduce on high, lid off
Reduce @&(~1)stew{} on high with the lid off for ~reduce{25%min}.
